# {{ package_name or project_name }}

Replace this body with the skill's instructions. The frontmatter `description` is what an
agent matches against when it decides whether to load the skill, so it says what the skill
does and when to use it, not what it is.

## Where a capability goes

OMP locates a skill at `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` without recursion, and identifies it by the
bare frontmatter `name`. Names deduplicate across every configured source and the first
match wins, so the owning plugin's name is the prefix that stops one resolving to someone
else's capability of the same name. This skill carries the plugin name itself; a second one
here goes under `skills/{{ package_name or project_name }}-<thing>/`, and the same rule
holds for `agents/<name>.md`, `commands/<name>.md`, and `rules/<name>.md`.
`scripts/build_catalog.py` refuses a capability that breaks it.

Long skills split their detail into `references/*.md` beside this file and link to it, so
the always-loaded body stays short. This starter ships none; add them as the skill grows.
